third
party guarantee. Credit Guarantee Scheme for MSEs of CGTMSE does not stipulate any condition
with regard to selection of the beneficiary, sanction, disbursement, fol
low up and recovery of loans by
its MLIs. These are as per the extant guidelines of the respective MLIs.
To enhance access to credit for MSMEs through digital platforms and other innovative
mechanisms for facilitating MSMEs, Trade Receivables e Disc
ounting System (TReDS), an electronic
platform, facilitates the discounting of trade receivables of MSMEs through multiple financiers. To
unlock their working capital by converting their trade receivables into cash the Government of India has
announced to
reduce the turnover threshold of buyers for mandatory onboarding on the TReDS platform
from Rs. 500 crore to Rs. 250 crore.
Grievances are directly received in CGTMSE or through the Ministry of MSME by post/mail
and are redressed suitably.
