The 66th Report of the Standing Committee on Finance emphasized the urgent need to rationalize the
rate of GST on insurance products, particularly health and term insurance, which is currently set at 18%.
The report highlighted that high GST rate significantly contributes to the overall premium burden,
making insurance less accessible and deterring individuals from purchasing policies. To address this
