J0277,Q06,is interest on loans exempt from GST,R-GST-C-111,View,"Schedule II of the CGST Act, 2017, it is > 2. Making loans more affordable by","by
NBFC in co -lending arrangements
are purely in the nature of interest
on loan and are not a consideration
for any service, and thus are not
subject to the levy of GST.
• There are two models of co -lending.
These models are referred to as Co-
Origination (CLM -1) and Co -Lending
(CLM-2). These models are broadly
covered under Circulars dated
21/09/2018 and 05/11/2020,
respectively, issued by RBI. While the
former arrangement entails joint
contribution of credit at the facility
level by both the lenders as also
sharing of risks and rewards, the latter
model, which has superseded the
former, entails disbursement by the
NBFC itself, with banks taking on their
share of the loan on their books on a
back-to-back basis. In the co -lending
model, banks can also choose to either
mandatorily take their share of
individual loans originated by NBFCs
or to retain the discretion to reject
certain loans after due diligence.
• During the examination of the issue, it
was seen that there are several types
of agreements between banks and
NBFCs in co -lending arrangements.
The Fitment Committee was of the
view that the structures/practices in
these agreements need to be examined
in more detail before a decision can
be taken in the matter.
• After deliberations, Fitment
Committee recommended to defer
the issue.
