Penal charges represent charges over and above the normal interest rates/fees levied for default/breach by the Borrower in complying with the material terms of the loan contract. The intent of levying penal charges is essentially to instil a sense of financial discipline and discourage borrowers from defaulting on their obligations, as specified in the loan contract or facility agreement.
