What KYC and documentation are required?
To complete
TReDS Registration Online
on a
TReDS Platform
like
M1xchange TReDS
, entities need to submit basic KYC and business documents. These generally include proof of identity, proof of business existence, bank details, and authorised signatory information. The documentation requirements vary slightly based on whether you are an MSME, corporate, or financier. Once registered, users can access the
TReDS Portal
through their TReDS Login to upload documents and begin transactions. For the complete list of required documents, please refer to the list here [
https://www.m1xchange.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/KYC-Documents-Requirement-List-1.pdf
].
Who is mandated to register on TReDS?
As per government directives, all corporates with a turnover of ₹250 crore and above are mandated to complete
TReDS Registration
. They must register on any RBI-approved
TReDS Platform
, such as
M1xchange TReDS
, to enable their MSME suppliers to access timely payments. This mandate ensures financial inclusion and better liquidity for small businesses.
