settlement1. What is Invoicemart?
Invoicemart is an online platform owned and maintained by A.Treds Ltd. It is based on the Trade Receivables Discounting System (TReDS), introduced by the RBI to improve cash flow for MSMEs through factoring and reverse factoring. Invoicemart connects buyers, MSME sellers and financiers to help MSMEs receive faster payments for their invoices.2. What is A.Treds Ltd?
A.Treds Ltd. is a joint venture between Axis Bank and mjunction services. It is licensed by the RBI to operate a Trade Receivables Discounting System (TReDS) platform under the Payment and Settlement Systems Act, 20073. What is the objective of Invoicemart?
The objective of Invoicemart is to facilitate MSMEs receive early payment by enabling financing of their invoices through factoring. This helps businesses to improve cash flow, gain quicker access to working capital and reduce dependence on traditional borrowing methods, thereby supporting business growth and operational efficiency.4. Who can participate on Invoicemart?
The following participants can register on Invoicemart:
MSME sellers (suppliers)
Corporate and other buyers (including Government Departments and PSUs)
Financiers (Banks, NBFC Factors and other Financial Institutions as permitted by the RBI)5. How does factoring work?
Factoring helps suppliers receive payments faster for the goods or services they provide. It works by introducing a financier between the MSME seller and the buyer. The financier provides funds to the MSME seller against the invoice or bill of exchange raised on the buyer.6. How does reverse factoring work?
In reverse factoring, the buyer creates the invoice on the platform, unlike factoring where the seller creates it. The financier provides funds to the MSME Seller against the invoice or bill of exchange raised on the buyer.7. Does the platform support both factoring and reverse factoring?
Yes. The platform supports both factoring and reverse factoring transactions.8. Does the platform support suppliers from the services sector as well?
Yes. The platform supports MSMEs operating in both the manufacturing and services sectors.9. How is Invoicemart different from traditional invoice discounting?
Traditional invoice discounting usually requires a separate agreement between the buyer, seller and financier for each business relationship. This can make the process time-consuming and complex.
With Invoicemart TReDS, sellers, buyers and financiers transact through a single platform with a one-time agreement, eliminating the need for separate agreements for each relationship and simplifying the invoice financing process.
With
Invoicemart (TReDS):
Participants sign a one-time agreement with the platform, and there is no need to sign an agreement for each and every transaction.
Multiple financiers can",,,,,,
