account which offers certain minimum facilities, free of charge, to the holders of such
accounts with an objective of deepening financial inclusion. In order to provide
affordable banking facilities to public, to drive enhanced usage of BSBD accounts and
also in the interest of better customer service for BSBD account holders, it was decided
to review the extant instructions on BSBD account and accordingly, the draft Reserve
Bank of India (Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account) Directions, 2025 w as i ssued on
October 1, 2025 for public consultation / feedback. The public / stakeholder feedback
received has since been analysed and it has been decided to issue the final
instructions on BSBD account to commercial banks (excluding Small Finance Banks,
Payments Banks and Local Area Banks) (hereinafter individually referred to as a
‘bank’) through amendment to the Reserve Bank of India (Commercial Banks -
Responsible Business Conduct) Directions, 2025.
