“86. The Basic Savings Bank Deposit (BSBD) Account is designed as a savings
account to provide affordable banking facilities to the public at large. Every bank
shall offer a BSBD account which shall be considered a normal banking service
available to all.  A bank shall offer the following basic minimum facilities in a BSBD
account, free of charge, without any requirement of minimum balance to be
maintained in such an account.
(1) Deposit of cash.
(2) Receipt of money through any electronic channel or deposit / collection of
cheques.
(3) No limit on number and value of deposits that can be made in a month.
