Participations with interest to the participating bank irrespective of the default if any in
the advance in question.143. Accounting: The issuing bank will show the amount of Participations as
borrowing while the participating bank shall show the same under Advances to bank
i.e. due from banks. The Participations would be treated as part of the net Demand
and Time Liabilities and net bank balances for purposes of statutory reserve
requirements.
144. Reporting of Data: As a result of outstanding Participations being treated as
