J1068,Q24,Udyam registration certificate for PSL benefits,R-SANSAD-038,Rajya Sabha Unstarred Q. 1548 (05 Aug 2024): Credit Card Scheme for MSMEs,UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 1548,"UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 1548TO BE ANSWERED ON 05.08.2024
CREDIT CARD SCHEME FOR MSMEs
1548SHRI MUKUL BALKRISHNA W ASNIK:
Will the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:
whether it is a fact that large numbers of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs)
have not yet entered the formal financial system and continue to depend on informal f
inancial
sector for their financial requirements
;
if so, the estimated extent to which the MSMEs are dependent on the informal financial
sector
;
whether Government will consider to introduce a Credit Card Scheme for MSMEs in line
with the Kisan C
redit Card (KCC) Scheme of National Bank for Agriculture and Rural
Development (NABARD)
; and
if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?
(a
and (b):
The
Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) launched Udyam
Registration Portal (URP) on 01.07.2020
for formalisation of MSMEs
. Subsequently, Uydam
Assist Platform (UAP) was launched on 11.01.2023 to formalize Informal Micro Enter
prises
(IMEs). IMEs having Udyam Assist Certificate are treated at par with Micro Enterprises only for
the purpose of availing Priority Sector Lending benefits. As on 31.07.2024, 4.78 crore
Enterprises are registered on URP, including 1.99 crore IMEs. The
formalized Enterprises are
eligible to avail the benefit of various schemes of Government of India for providing financial
support like Credit Guarantee Scheme, Self Reliant India (SRI) Fund etc. subject to meeting the
eligibility conditions.
(c) and (d):
The Ministry of MSME in association with National Payment Corporation of
India (NPCI) launched the MSME Rupay Credit Card on pilot basis for Udyam registered
MSMEs in year 2022.",,,,,,
J1069,Q24,Udyam registration certificate for PSL benefits,R-SANSAD-070,Lok Sabha Unstarred Q. 2847 (08 Aug 2024): Udyam Assist Platform,LOK SABHA,"LOK SABHAUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 2847TO BE ANSWERED ON 08.08.2024UDYAM ASSIST PLATFORM
2847.SMT. SANDHYA RAY:
Will the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:
the number of registrations received on the Udyam Assist Platform, State/UT
wise;
whether the Informal Micro Enterprises(IMEs) which register on the platform would be
penalized for not having a GST Number;
whether the Udyam Assist Platform provides Priority Sector Lending (PSL) benefits to
registered IMEs; and
if so, the details thereof and if not,  the reasons therefor?MINISTER OF STATE FOR MICRO,SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES
(a):
The State/UT
wise details of registration on Udyam Assist Platform (UAP), as on July 30,
2024, are given at Annexure.
