reasons such as change in the company owner, certificate not required anymore, duplicate registration,
shut down of enterprises and other reasons. In the last 3 years, the numbe r of MSME’s registered on
Udyam Registration Portal (URP) and Udyam Assist Platform (UAP) has increased from 1.65 crore (as
on 01.04.2023) to 8.84 crore (as on 30.06.2026). The number of MSMEs  closed/shut down  as a
proportion of those which have registered in the last three years is only 1,21,805 which is 0.19%. The
State/UT-wise number of enterprises registered and de-registered/shut-down during the last three years
are at Annexure-I.
Government of India has notified Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS) 5.0 on
05.05.2026 with an aim to infuse additional credit of Rs. 2.55 lakh crore to existing borrower s. Out of
the total outlay under ECLGS 5.0, Rs. 2 lakh crore is earmarked for MSMEs. There is a prov ision of
extending 100% guarantee coverage to MSMEs and 90% to other business segments . As on 14.07.2026,
since launch of the scheme, 4,65,807 guarantees  worth Rs.1,72,526 crore have been issued. The scheme
has benefited India's MSME sector wherein 98% of  all guarantees issued (by number) and 82% of the
total guaranteed amount is towards the MSMEs.
