Revalidate the bank accounts that were
returned as invalid IFSC from Canara Bank
during the period from 28/10/2024 to
29/11/2024 due to Data sync up issue at
Canara Bank end.
On 28/10/2024, GSTN went live with
Canara Bank for the real time bank account
validation. For some days, it was observed
that for valid IFSC codes also, we were
getting Invalid IFSC as response from
Canara Bank end.
Due to this, even for valid account details
(Account number / IFSC), taxpayers were
getting Invalid IFSC response and same
was updated in the ACCT_DETL table,
once the non- core amendment application
was submitted.
The same was conveyed to Canara Bank
and they did fix on 29/11/2024.
The issue was with Canara bank, the
Canara Bank rejected various a/c validation
requests containing correct IFSC code, once
correction was done at Canara Bank, we re -
initiated the affected a/c numbers for
revalidation via data fix.
Data fix
is done.
Page 241 of 376
Discussion:
EVP, GSTN stated that this issue related to data sync between Canara Bank (via NPCI) and the GSTN
database, where a glitch caused the validation of even valid bank accounts to fail, resulting in
incorrect “invalid IFSC” error messages. These errors were recorded in the account detail tables,
causing difficulties for taxpayers in validating their bank accounts. To resolve this, a data fix was
applied, and 1,778 bank accounts were revalidated. The matter was placed before the ITGRC for
approval.
Decision: ITGRC took note of the data fix done by the GSTN.
