Q1. What is the objective of SIDBI's Project Funding facility?
SIDBI's Project Funding facility is a SIDBI project loan that provides MSME project finance, enabling Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) to finance project-based funding, including the setting up of new units, expansion and modernisation. Assistance is extended under Direct Credit Scheme.
Q2. What quantum of assistance is available under Direct Credit Scheme?
Up to ₹100 crore with up to 75% of total project cost in case of existing entity and 67% in case of new entity.
Q3. Who is eligible to avail Project Funding from SIDBI?
Both new and existing MSMEs with valid Udyam Registration, with a satisfactory credit history and no defaults to any bank or financial institution, are eligible to apply.
Q4. What is the repayment period applicable to project loans?
Flexible repayment tenure as per project requirements.
Q5. How can an enterprise apply for Project Funding?
A SIDBI project loan for MSMEs can be applied online. Applications are submitted through the ""Apply Now"" option on the SIDBI website, which opens the Bank's online loan application portal. Enterprises that need assistance in filing the application may approach nearest SIDBI Branch Office or a Referral Partner registered with SIDBI. For queries, call the toll-free number
